{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_298aa49449ca42a6869151a1e905cecbeeb70ec483dac8ea42332403613b2f2d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, and Rust dependency license policy is enforced via cargo deny configured in deny.toml."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2fa82defceb6b657527159a20818cff13f31664cc44bc90f22bb675ac4b9c273"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A typed app-server boundary exposes the local Rust runtime to the desktop; the Tauri shell stays project-aware while the runtime owns thread execution, model calls, tools, state, and live events."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60f4b8e396cf16f26efef8bca8e617537b02d7e8120fe96379715a395f23400b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The memory system supports automatic prompt recall, explicit memory tools, candidate saves, local promote/archive/forget flows, and audit state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_73b8abcfc4bcace2d4eef3909a6d42d70d53bdc8084b051ed31836579b0f9edd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each thread runs behind an actor-backed ThreadRuntime that serializes turns while streaming snapshots, status, and events back to the GUI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_847e79c694dfa5a025b03991ded40c5a58c15365f1aa79bfaa55dbb9f8ab2733"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project states it currently targets personal workstation use, with non-goals including production-grade sandbox isolation, hosted collaboration, and a stable public SDK."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8adf95349c5360a706a6f293ca66e49b04d0ac4912b54632bc1d26daabc64700"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent policy gates both tool visibility and execution; tool contracts live in src/tools while per-turn orchestration lives in src/runtime/tool."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8db05fe039abe8bf3c7748d54d0cfe1ce3968ddbd79a8bc21fddc178bee1bb3f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Local durability is append-first: each thread has a rollout.jsonl ledger, and IndexDb stores cross-thread indexes for projects, threads, goals, memory, and review state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b246bd719e68dffb364351d2812e94dc8b77841c791738109d13dc6bc7240379"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run npm ci, tauri:dev, test, and build commands, plus cargo test, fmt, clippy, and cargo deny checks for verification."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c591f429ce11725d0ecf9d96667a542347a3cbe8ff03f98460dea8b492012332"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The model layer normalizes provider-specific APIs into internal conversation, tool-call, multimodal, reasoning, and streaming types."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ec655c89135001641b1a84c96b750ee762cb65a7cf6d01cb2c890735a08e424b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ExAgent is a desktop-first agent workbench with a Rust runtime and Tauri/React GUI, aimed at long-running coding work in local projects with resumable sessions."}],"claim_ids":["clm_298aa49449ca42a6869151a1e905cecbeeb70ec483dac8ea42332403613b2f2d","clm_2fa82defceb6b657527159a20818cff13f31664cc44bc90f22bb675ac4b9c273","clm_60f4b8e396cf16f26efef8bca8e617537b02d7e8120fe96379715a395f23400b","clm_73b8abcfc4bcace2d4eef3909a6d42d70d53bdc8084b051ed31836579b0f9edd","clm_847e79c694dfa5a025b03991ded40c5a58c15365f1aa79bfaa55dbb9f8ab2733","clm_8adf95349c5360a706a6f293ca66e49b04d0ac4912b54632bc1d26daabc64700","clm_8db05fe039abe8bf3c7748d54d0cfe1ce3968ddbd79a8bc21fddc178bee1bb3f","clm_b246bd719e68dffb364351d2812e94dc8b77841c791738109d13dc6bc7240379","clm_c591f429ce11725d0ecf9d96667a542347a3cbe8ff03f98460dea8b492012332","clm_ec655c89135001641b1a84c96b750ee762cb65a7cf6d01cb2c890735a08e424b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:07:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_eb7679b0425847648add0411ddf6185d","id":"pg_1e3a872417f158ab8893092c80f26a1b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/exqqstar-exagent-readme-md-d9adbbd6f18a-092c80f26a1b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9f7165dbd30150229fafd313055e6bc0"],"title":"exqqstar/ExAgent/README.md @ d9adbbd6f18a","updated_at":"2026-0